<title>USA: RTRS-USDA lifts Australia wheat crop forecast to 19.5 million tonnes.</title>
<headline>RTRS-USDA lifts Australia wheat crop forecast to 19.5 million tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>World grain crops will total 1,820.43 million tonnes in 1996/97, up from 1,702.20 million in 1995/96, the U.S. Agriculture Department said Wednesday, raising the 1996/97 estimate from last month's 1,802.35 million.</p>
<p>It raised its Australian wheat crop forecast for 1996/97 to 19.5 million tonnes from 17.5 million tonnes in August.</p>
<p>USDA forecast the world wheat crop at 579.50 million tonnes, coarse grains at 865.25 million, and rice at 375.68 million. Oilseed output was pegged at 253.38 million tonnes, and cotton at 87.35 million bales .</p>
<p>In 1995/96, the world grew 535.93 million tonnes of wheat, 794.99 million of coarse grains, 371.28 million of rice, 254.27 million of oilseeds, and 91.50 million bales of cotton.</p>
